    if planet == planet1 or planet == planet2:
        continue
    if planet in ["Saturn", "Uranus"] and planet1 < planet2:
        yield planet
    elif planet in ["Jupiter", "Neptune"] and planet2 < planet1:
        yield planet
    else:
        continue


Note: The range(1, 9) line is used to iterate over the list of planets in our solar system, starting from 1 (Mercury) and ending at 9 (Neptune). The if statements inside the loop are used to check if the current planet is either planet1 or planet2, and if it is, the loop continues to the next planet. If the current planet is not either planet1 or planet2, it is checked if it is in the list of planets between the two given planets, and if it is, it is yielded.

